2026-09-01T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Certificate lifetimes, from a risk-based ceiling
 # uuid: 486ba694-3235-54b3-b995-766cf7b0e809
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:details
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-01T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2145) 'every private CA and leaf the workspace issues.
 # tags: rfd:scope
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Each private CA and leaf gets a lifetime and a rotation cadence set by its risk.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2145) 'RFD66606-2134, RFD66606-2141, RFD66606-2142 landed with 10-year CAs and 1-to-2-year leaves.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2145) '2144 minted a 10-year WebTransport intermediate on the same pattern.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Check a new private CA or leaf against the lifetime table above before you issue it; the
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2145) 'sections below hold the citations and the audit.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Certificate lifetimes, from a risk-based ceiling
 # tags: rfd:details-title
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2145) '    role                              notAfter       rotate every
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2145) '    -----------------------------     ------------   ------------
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2145) '    Root CA (private, offline key)    25 years       5 years, policy
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2145) '    Break-glass CA (in 1P)            25 years       5 years, policy
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2145) '    Intermediate CA                   3 years        1 year
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2145) '    mTLS server + client (services)   90 days        <=45 days
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2145) '    WebTransport leaf                 14 days        <=10 days
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2145) '    Break-glass leaf (rare, gated)    2 years        on use, then revoke
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2145) 'The root's `notAfter` is 25 years because RFC 5280 §4.1.2.5 makes the
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2145) 'field MANDATORY, not because rotation should wait that long. Offline
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2145) 'root: tiny compromise surface, expensive downstream re-issuance.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Rotation is a **5-year policy commitment**, enforced by
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2145) '`check_anti_entropy.py`, not by cert validation. Intermediates and
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2145) 'leaves are the opposite: their `notAfter` IS the rotation gate.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2145) 'RFD66606-2134, RFD66606-2141, RFD66606-2142, RFD66606-2144. Each carries a retraction pointing
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2145) 'here.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2145) 'The second thing the guidance predates
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2145) 'The guidance also predates a Mozilla Root Store Policy that removes public trust
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2145) 'after 15 years of key material.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Why the root cert has an expiry at all
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2145) 'RFC 5280 §4.1.2.5 makes `notAfter` a MANDATORY field on every X.509
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2145) 'certificate. There is no valid X.509 leaf, intermediate, or root that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2145) 'carries no expiry. So the question is not "should the root have an
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2145) 'expiry" but "how far out do we set the field that has to be there".
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2145) '    The validity period for a certificate is the period of time from
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2145) '    notBefore through notAfter, inclusive. […] To indicate that a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2145) '    certificate has no well-defined expiration date, the notAfter
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2145) '    SHOULD be assigned the GeneralizedTime value of
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2145) '    99991231235959Z.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2145) '    (RFC 5280 §4.1.2.5)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2145) 'RFC 5280 permits the "never expires" sentinel (`99991231235959Z`) for
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2145) 'certs the issuer treats as having no defined end date. Some private
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2145) 'CAs use it. This RFD does not, for the reasons below. First, OpenSSL prints
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2145) '`notAfter=Dec 31 23:59:59 9999 GMT` and some X.509 parsers reject the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2145) 'year field as out of range: RFC 5280 requires UTCTime for years
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2145) '1950-2049 and GeneralizedTime after, so pre-1994 parsers and some
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2145) 'embedded stacks fail. Second, the intent ("this cert never expires,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2145) 'we rotate on schedule") is invisible to anyone reading the cert.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2145) '25 years is long enough that the field is not the rotation gate, and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2145) 'short enough that every stack we ship to handles it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Why the ROTATION on the root is 5 years, not 25
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Three converging bodies of guidance land in the same window.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2145) '**Mozilla Root Store Policy §7.1** removes public-trust for a root CA
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2145) 'whose key material is more than 15 years old:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2145) '    For a Root CA certificate trusted for server authentication,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2145) '    Mozilla will remove the websites trust bit when the CA key
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2145) '    material is more than 15 years old.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2145) '    (Mozilla Root Store Policy v2.9, 2023-09)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Our root is private, so Mozilla does not force our hand. The industry
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2145) 'consensus reflected in that number is that 15 years is the outer edge
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2145) 'before cryptographic parameters and operational discipline drift
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2145) 'enough to warrant re-mint.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2145) '**NCSC in-house PKI principles: "keep certificate lifetimes as short
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2145) 'as practical".** No fixed year on the root. The phrasing is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2145) 'deliberate. Short as practical, taking rotation cost into account.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2145) '    Certificates should have lifetimes that are as short as practical,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2145) '    while balancing the operational overhead of renewal.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2145) '    (NCSC "In-house public key infrastructure, PKI principles")
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2145) '**NIST SP 800-57 Part 1 §5.3.6 (key lifetimes).** Recommends both
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2145) '"originator usage period" and "recipient usage period" bounded.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Public-key signing keys used to certify other keys are the highest-
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2145) 'value keys in the system and thus have the tightest recommended
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2145) 'cryptoperiod. Not a specific year, but a directional bound.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Five years is the smallest rotation cadence at which the CA ceremony
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2145) 'is a set-piece event we prepare for rather than an emergency. Half of
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2145) 'that is the "start scheduling the next ceremony" trigger.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Why the break-glass CA gets the SAME numbers as the root
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2145) 'The break-glass CA sits in 1P beside the operator's other credentials
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2145) 'and comes out on the day the primary root is unusable. That day is a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-2145) 'disaster with a fixed script. The break-glass root immediately signs
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-2145) 'a new set of intermediates and every downstream leaf. If the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-2145) 'break-glass has less validity remaining than the primary rotation
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-2145) 'cadence, the swap-in re-mints twice (once to swap, once to reach the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-2145) 'next scheduled ceremony). That is the class of error a DR runbook
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:40Z (RFD66606-2145) 'cannot afford.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:41Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:42Z (RFD66606-2145) 'So the break-glass CA carries the SAME `notAfter` as the primary
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:43Z (RFD66606-2145) 'root (25 years) and the SAME policy rotation window (5 years). It
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:44Z (RFD66606-2145) 'also carries a bigger compromise surface than the primary root
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:45Z (RFD66606-2145) 'because 1P is warmer storage than an offline HSM ceremony. Its
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:46Z (RFD66606-2145) 'audit expectation is stricter: `op` reads are logged, the 1P item
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:47Z (RFD66606-2145) 'is CONCEALED-only (RFD66606-2144 defect #12 was moving the key from
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:48Z (RFD66606-2145) '`notesPlain` to CONCEALED), and any pull of the private key is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:49Z (RFD66606-2145) 'followed by a `shred -u` of the scratch file.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:50Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:51Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Why the intermediates get 3 years
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:52Z (RFD66606-2145) 'An intermediate CA is online (or at least reachable) whenever it signs
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:53Z (RFD66606-2145) 'a leaf. Its compromise surface is bigger than the root's. Rotating it
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:54Z (RFD66606-2145) 'under 5 years is standard private-PKI practice. 3 years keeps the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:55Z (RFD66606-2145) 'cadence at "annual re-mint of a new one, run for a year, retire the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:56Z (RFD66606-2145) 'older one". A two-CA overlap window costs nothing and lets the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:57Z (RFD66606-2145) 'trust-store update propagate.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:58Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:59Z (RFD66606-2145) 'CA/B Forum's SC-081v3 vote (2025-04) sets public TLS leaf lifetimes on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:00Z (RFD66606-2145) 'a schedule (200 days now, 100 by 2027-03, 47 by 2029-03). The root
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:01Z (RFD66606-2145) 'and intermediate lifetimes for publicly-trusted CAs are already
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:02Z (RFD66606-2145) '15 years (Mozilla). Our private intermediates run inside that number,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:03Z (RFD66606-2145) 'at 1/5 of it, because we control the whole chain and can rotate
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:04Z (RFD66606-2145) 'cheaply.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:05Z (RFD66606-2145) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:06Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Why the leaves get 90 days / 14 days
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:07Z (RFD66606-2145) '**mTLS server + client (services): 90 days.** Aligns with the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:08Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Let's Encrypt cadence the industry has run for a decade without
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:02:09Z (RFD66606-2145) 'incident. Matches CA/B Forum's 2027 target for public TLS. Short
 # tags: rfd:details
